{"id":"fence","name":"Fence","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:fence"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Fence","text":"(Heb. gader), Num. 22:24 (R.V.). Fences were constructions of unmortared stones, to protect gardens, vineyards, sheepfolds, etc. From various causes they were apt to bulge out and fall (Ps. 62:3). In Ps. 80:12, R.V. (see Isa. 5:5), the psalmist says, “Why hast thou broken down her fences?” Serpents delight to lurk in the crevices of such fences (Eccl. 10:8; comp. Amos 5:19)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1447","lemma":"גָּדֵר","xlit":"gâdêr","gloss":"a circumvallation","kjv":"fence, hedge, wall","count":7,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H4881","lemma":"מְשׂוּכָה","xlit":"mᵉsûwkâh","gloss":"a hedge","kjv":"hedge","count":2,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H3754","lemma":"כֶּרֶם","xlit":"kerem","gloss":"a garden or vineyard","kjv":"vines, vineyard, vintage. See also H1021","count":3,"share":0.21},{"strong":"H1443","lemma":"גָּדַר","xlit":"gâdar","gloss":"to wall in or around","kjv":"close up, fence up, hedge, inclose","count":2,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H6555","lemma":"פָּרַץ","xlit":"pârats","gloss":"to break out","kjv":"abroad, breach, break, burst out","count":2,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H1129","lemma":"בָּנָה","xlit":"bânâh","gloss":"to build","kjv":"build, obtain children, make, repair","count":2,"share":0.14}],"verses":["Num.22.24","Ps.62.3","Eccl.10.8","Isa.5.5","Ezek.22.30","Hos.2.6","Mic.7.11","Prov.15.19","Prov.24.30","Prov.24.31","Song.4.12","Isa.5.2","Nah.3.17","Matt.21.33"],"related":[{"id":"hedges","type":"cooccur","shared":9,"jaccard":0.333,"why":"9 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"hedge","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.19,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"vineyards","type":"cooccur","shared":6,"jaccard":0.091,"why":"6 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"vineyard","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.077,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"slothfulness","type":"cooccur","sh